    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Gujarati, Punjabi, Kannada, Malayalam & Odia — five more Indic scripts",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Rendered with --font gu --font pa --font kn --font ml --font or --font latin --lang gu,pa,kn,ml,or,latin. pdfnative 1.9.0 routes these five scripts through its Indic engine (32 scripts in all): Kannada vowel signs precede the subjoined consonants, a legacy Malayalam chillu (consonant + virama + ZWJ) draws the chillu glyph, every part of a two-part vowel sign names its code point, and a sentence-final danda keeps an Odia or Gurmukhi line on its own shaper. Untagged output carries each reordered run as /ActualText, so extract-text returns the source text without --tagged."
    },
